   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Merging a list of data frames",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<div>Mike&#39;s answer is much more complete, but I use the bind_rows function often. I would use a simplified version of what Mike sent, it will include NAs for non-matches...not sure if that&#39;s what you are after. Using same example data:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">library(dplyr)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">df.list&lt;-bind_rows(l) # add NAs for non-matches</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">df.all&lt;-merge(df.list, target_df, by=&quot;id&quot;) # merge by &quot;id&quot;</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">head(dff)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><div>  id      CH4 CO2 NOX col1 col2</div><div>1  1 2.572637  NA  NA    v    N</div><div>2  2 2.344085  NA  NA    r    T</div><div>3  3 2.080344  NA  NA    w    A</div><div>4  4 2.783236  NA  NA    x    O</div><div>5  5 2.624123  NA  NA    y    E</div><div>6  6 2.135638  NA  NA    s    C</div></font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>Adios,</div><div>Ryan</div><div><br></div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Saturday, December 5, 2015 at 10:46:02 PM UTC-8, Michael Koontz wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
