     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<div>Mike&#39;s answer is much more complete, but I use the bind_rows function often. I would use a simplified version of what Mike sent, it will include NAs for non-matches...not sure if that&#39;s what you are after. Using same example data:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(dplyr)</font></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">df.list&lt;-bind_rows(l) # add NAs for non-matches</font></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">df.all&lt;-merge(df.list, target_df, by=&quot;id&quot;) # merge by &quot;id&quot;</font></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">head(dff)</font></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" face=\"courier new, monospace\"><div>  id      CH4 CO2 NOX col1 col2</div><div>1  1 2.572637  NA  NA    v    N</div><div>2  2 2.344085  NA  NA    r    T</div><div>3  3 2.080344  NA  NA    w    A</div><div>4  4 2.783236  NA  NA    x    O</div><div>5  5 2.624123  NA  NA    y    E</div><div>6  6 2.135638  NA  NA    s    C</div></font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>Adios,</div><div>Ryan</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
