     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div>I have a list of data frames that all look like this, except the third column which has different names.</div><div>the names of the elements of the list are the header of the third column<br><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div>   id area      CH4</div><div>1 132 7339 2.122865</div><div>2 131 7279 2.107544</div><div>3 130 7086 2.058260</div><div>4 129 7288 2.109842</div><div>5 128 7280 2.107799</div><div>6 127 7221 2.092733</div></div></code></div><br> I want to merge the third column of all data frames in the list to another existing data frame by the &quot;id&quot; column.</div></div><div>So that I get a data frame with the first column &quot;id&quot; followed by &quot;CH4&quot;....</div><div>The left_join only works on data frames and not lists.</div><div>lapply with merge gives me a list of merged data frames</div><div><br></div><div>It seems like there should be an easy way but I can&#39;t find it on google or think of one.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nCheck out our R resources at <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467657385000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0AHePgCkoEdaXoGodX03j0\">http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;D