   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">You can use the tidyr functions to ‘spread’ the data back out into short form (each gas will have its own column) after you’ve merged. I think I forgot to keep the ‘gas’ column in the filter() function call, so that is different in this script also.<div><br></div><div>Does this get you what you are looking for? Are there better ways for filtering out the NAs?</div><div><br></div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div>library(dplyr)</div><div>library(tidyr)</div><div><br></div><div>df1 &lt;- data.frame(id=1:6, area=c(7339, 7279, 7086, 7288, 7280, 7221),  CH4=2+runif(6))</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div>df2 &lt;- data.frame(id=1:6, area=c(7339, 7279, 7086, 7288, 7280, 7221),  CO2=2+runif(6))</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div>df3 &lt;- data.frame(id=1:6, area=c(7339, 7279, 7086, 7288, 7280, 7221),  NOX=2+runif(6))</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><br></div><div>target_df &lt;- data.frame(id=1:18, col1=sample(letters, 18), col2=sample(LETTERS, 18))</div><div><br></div><div>l &lt;- list(df1, df2, df3)</div><div><br></div><div>long_form &lt;- l %&gt;%</div><div>  bind_rows() %&gt;% # Collapse the list into a data.frame. Use dplyr to allow different column names</div><div>  gather(key=gas, value=measurement, -id, -area) %&gt;% # Convert to long form</div><div>  filter(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467657387000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3rpQoD9T_dfoKdidrvJdHS\">is.na</a>(measurement)) %&gt;% # Only keep complete cases</div></div></div>"
